15535	2	32549	Continuous Diagnostic Device for Pin Insulators	The paper describes the pin insulators diagnostic device controlling its leakage current and signalizing if a defect occurred. The insulator condition is assessed under operating voltage using leakage current monitoring. A laboratory device sample has been made. The device compares input and reference (regulated) voltage signals using a comparator. Besides, the scheme contains a diode bridge protecting a comparator from overvoltage. Several experiments were performed. Different types of insulators were mounted on a shunt and high alternating voltage was applied to the insulators. Leakage current was taken from the shunt structure. The monitored value of the leakage current corresponds to the value of the insulation normal resistance limit. Insulators with different defects were used in the tests: aluminum powder, soot, dust and artificial defect in the form of graphite line. As a result of the work, the operability of the developed device is confirmed. Probably, the next step of the work is the development of the diagnostic device signal transmission system connecting to substation for the personnel control. © 2022 IEEE.	2022-01-01	t	0.6666666666666666
