но как уточнением активных сопротивлений, так и учетом изменения токов под влиянием температур.Mathematical models of the steady-state of a loop network with duplicate supply including the equations for network nodal voltages and line heat balance equation are developed. We consider three possible algorithms of numerical solution for the steady-state equations based on Newton's method which differ in the way of temperature adjusting. It is shown that direct solution of the whole system of equations by Newton's method is inefficient because of the low convergence and the best performance is obtained by the method based on the temperature correction carried out at each step of iterative solution of nodal voltages equations. Accounting for the temperature dependence of the resistance can significantly improve the accuracy of currents, voltage fluctuation and power loss in the network. The refinement of the power loss may exceed 40 % due to more precise determination of active resistance and temperature-induced changes in currents.▼Показать полностью	2015-01-01	t	0.5
