16311	2	31991	Analysis of electrophysical processes in system of interdigitated microelectrodes used in microchannels	The method of modeling the potential distribution in a system of interdigitated electrodes used for measurement DC resistance in a microchannel with liquid medium is presented. The method is based on the selection from this system the unit subdomain whose structure is substituted by an equivalent one. In its turn, the equivalent structure of the unit subdomain is divided into three rectangular regions. For each region, the analytical expression for the potential distribution is determined using the eigenfunction method. Each current density on the boundaries between the adjacent regions and on the boundaries with the electrodes is defined as the sum of orthogonal functions with unknown weighting coefficients. To find the unknown weighting coefficients the adjoint boundary conditions on the boundaries are used. In general, the determination of the weighting coefficients is reduced to solving a system of linear equations. The present method is applied to determine the potential distribution in the realistic system of the interdigitated microelectrodes used in the microchannel and the dependency of the resistance of the system of the interdigitated microelectrodes on the channel height. © 2016 IEEE.	2017-01-01	t	1
