18100	1	29302	Study of the Influence of the Main Parameters on the Mass and Efficiency the Switched-Reluctance Motor Drive Spindle	One of the problems that is solved in the development of the valve-inductor drive is to obtain the optimal parameters for a given criterion of the engine. In the design of the engine for the electric test, it is necessary to determine the degree of influence of its parameters on the main quality indicators for the purpose and conditions of operation: efficiency and weight. Given the large number of independent variables and limitations for optimization calculations, it is convenient to use algorithms based on the methods of circuit theory, as well as optimization methods that reduce the amount of calculations. The article deals with the formulation of the optimal design problem, substantiates the accepted optimality criteria, specifies the limits of changes in independent variables and restrictions that must be taken into account when searching for optimal engine options. The results of the calculations allow to determine the optimal efficiency or weight variants of the engines, as well as to determine the com-promissory variants, appointing one of the main criteria.	2019-01-01	t	\N
