18202	1	32976	Living Standards of Russians Will Twofold Deteriorate	After having attended the Moscow Economic Forum I was surprised to find that among a vast number of participants I failed to meet at least one who would share the opinion that the government of Russia has an elaborate economic policy. The majority of participants are sharing the opinion that the authorities are enthralled by illusions. There was a belief that oil prices would not fall below 80 dollars per barrel, but they have fallen; that after accession of Crimea the West would not impose any sanctions, but they have imposed ones; that after imposition of sanctions we would obtain credits in Asia and the Chinese investments would flow in Russia, but there is no such flow; that after devaluation there would be no price rising, and the prices have risen, and etc.	2015-05-05	t	\N
